.TH KEYSWITCH 1 "September 2026" "KeySwitch 0.14.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keyswitch \- automatic keyboard layout correction for Ubuntu X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyswitch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B KeySwitch
observes keyboard events in the current X11 session, detects words entered in
the wrong English or Russian layout, changes the XKB group and replaces the
mistyped word.
.PP
By default, KeySwitch also checks the current word after 1.5 seconds without
typing, before a separator is entered. Idle correction can be disabled
independently in the application settings.
.PP
Detection is a precision-first hybrid. Hard guards and explicit user rules are
resolved before the optional classifier. Dictionaries, Hunspell and context
form the deterministic fallback; when the bundled local linear character
n-gram model is available, enabled and applicable, it is the sole statistical
decision after those guards. It must pass its calibrated trigger/direction
threshold; coverage and language scores are diagnostic only and cannot veto
that result. A negative model decision is not handed to the fallback for a
second chance.
Its KSLM schema 4 container stores int16 weights, independent EN-to-RU and
RU-to-EN Platt coefficients, exact calibrated-logit thresholds for every
trigger/direction pair and sorted uint64 membership fingerprints instead of a
weight-bucket
occupancy bitset. The Local linear
model setting disables this extra layer. Diagnostics report its version and
checksum, or an explicit safe fallback when the artifact cannot be loaded.
The deterministic fallback is used only for a disabled or unavailable model,
or when the longer normalized interpretation contains fewer than five
characters. Shorter tokens remain under deterministic guards and user rules;
training and external typo evaluation enforce the same limit.
Frozen three- and four-character bilingual collisions are retained only as
safety evidence for the valid-source pre-model guard.
.PP
Offline training uses 2097152 hash buckets and at most 64 deterministic FTRL
epochs. Feature schema v5 uses only the source and alternative raw tokens:
signed character 1-5-grams, direction, length and trigger. It ignores context,
every WordScore and every language-model score field. Real short-lived context
remains in the conservative detector heuristic and is not counted again in the
linear score. The trainer invokes the same runtime extractor with the same seeds
and n-gram orders for exact train/serve feature parity. Train-only character scorers remain checked
provenance but are not classifier inputs; this does not disable Hunspell in the
runtime deterministic ensemble. Physical signatures use the
keyswitch:intent-v20:physical-signature split namespace. Identity and typo
signatures that cross splits, languages or protected safety rows are
quarantined before row creation.
.PP
Schema 13 also consumes a byte-frozen, model-blind v20 hard-negative source.
Its 5000 EN and 5000 RU physical signatures are assigned under an independent
namespace as 3500/500/500/500 words per language across train, development,
calibration and threshold, with no test role. The loader verifies source and
Hunspell provenance, physical equivalence, uniqueness, exact role sizes and
the SHA-256 of all 120000 re-expanded symmetric rows before the full leakage
audit. External provenance indexes the base lexical and safety dataset first,
then adds this development domain exactly once to the independent holdout
exclusions. The independent holdout uses different namespaces.
.PP
Calibration, threshold and sealed-test splits use neutral context as their
primary slice. Fixed non-empty label-independent context-stress profiles prove
feature-schema-v5 invariance: changing context must not alter the vector, logit
or decision, and every profile must pass the same per-trigger gates.
.PP
Before sealed-test evaluation, separate EN-to-RU/RU-to-EN thresholds are
selected jointly for every trigger with neutral context. Each directional
operating curve requires both labels in its overall and typo slices. Aggregate
precision, recall and specificity
must reach 0.9995, 0.956 and 0.999; the typo slice must reach 0.9995, 0.91 and
0.999. The 12 primary selection FPR checks use a Bonferroni-corrected
family-wise 95 percent Wilson endpoint with per-comparison confidence
0.9958333333333333 and z-score 2.8652602385321333; it must not exceed 0.001.
In addition, training config schema 13 gives each trigger an exact selection
budget of zero false positives across the overall and typo slices. This
absolute budget is enforced
before the sealed test is materialised.
Schema 13 then deterministically chooses on the threshold split the greatest
common calibrated-logit margin that preserves the complete selection policy.
The margin is bounded by a signed 2.0 cap fixed before v11 from the model-blind
development corpus. Schema 13 selects its effective value only on the frozen
threshold role, records it for every trigger, and recomputes selection metrics
against the hardened boundaries. The sealed test does not select the margin.
The sealed test independently uses ordinary 95 percent Wilson and recall
0.95/0.90. Selection for Pause uses recall 0.91, typo recall 0.86, while its
sealed gate keeps 0.90/0.85; the same FPR limit and a logit threshold in
each direction at least 0.5 above the strictest non-pause threshold in that
same direction. Infeasible selection stops before the sealed test. The sealed
test keeps an independent 0.999 minimum precision for both slices, so stricter
selection provides transfer headroom. The safety gate runs the guarded production detector;
raw model predictions and membership coverage are diagnostic only.
.PP
Runtime selects the exact threshold_logit by trigger and physical direction,
then compares the calibrated logit directly with it. Its sigmoid-derived
confidence is diagnostic
only and is never used for the decision.
.PP
Training provenance includes hashes of the frozen sources, configuration,
trainer, development-corpus freezer, runtime model code, layouts, language
scorer, detector, protected tokens and the frozen hard-negative source,
together with dataset, quarantine, train-only scorer and Python/platform
identity. Only a successful gated build publishes its pre-synced report,
artifact and manifest, in that order; the manifest is the final commit marker
and process failures roll back replaced outputs. The model card documents the
two-run byte-identical retraining check. Training config schema 13, KSLM schema
4 and external publication manifest schema 1 are independent. Frozen external
evaluation additionally pins Hunspell dictionary and affix sizes and SHA-256
digests, expected lexical and unknown-typo corpus digests, at least 5000 words
per language, and all six runtime triggers.
.PP
Settings, exclusions, hotkeys, history and diagnostics are available from the
application window. Left-clicking the desktop indicator opens its native menu
with correction toggles, settings, history, exclusions, about and quit actions.
.PP
After a manual word conversion with Pause/Break, KeySwitch displays a focused
prompt above the input position. Enter immediately adds the conversion to the
local switching rules; Escape dismisses the offer. Local learning and its
fallback repeated-conversion threshold are configurable in the application.
.PP
Pause/Break converts the unfinished word, the layout-dependent symbols typed
right after a word boundary (for example a Russian quote meant as "@"), or the
last completed word; once anything else was typed after that word, the key
only switches the layout. The typing pause that triggers idle correction is
configurable (1.5 seconds by default). Early layout switching rewrites the
beginning of a word as soon as its prefix is impossible in the current
language and clearly continues in the other one; the minimum prefix length is
configurable and the feature can be disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start without presenting the main window.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Probe the X11 RECORD, XTEST and XKB backend, print JSON and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed KeySwitch version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/keyswitch/config.json
User settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/keyswitch/history.jsonl
Correction history, when enabled.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/keyswitch/learning.json
Explicitly learned conversions and rejected automatic corrections.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/keyswitch/dictionaries/
Optional per-user Hunspell dictionaries.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/keyswitch/keyswitch.log
Application log. Detailed word-decision diagnostics are disabled by default
and can be enabled in the About page. They record decision and skip reasons,
shadow verdicts for protected words, layout-change attribution, deferred pause
corrections, early-switch events and settings changes. Diagnostic records may
contain typed words and application names; text from excluded applications is
redacted. The file is limited to 5 MiB and rotated with three backups.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/keyswitch/keyswitch/resources/models/layout_intent_v1.ksm
Bundled, checksum-validated KSLM schema 4 linear intent model, bounded to
14 MiB in total, with a 1 MiB embedded-manifest cap, a 12 MiB payload cap and
at most 2^20 exact membership fingerprints. The v1 filename identifies the
classifier generation.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/keyswitch/keyswitch/resources/models/en_US.lm
Frozen English lexical and character n-gram source used by the runtime scorer.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/keyswitch/keyswitch/resources/models/ru_RU.lm
Frozen Russian lexical and character n-gram source used by the runtime scorer.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display used for global input observation and correction.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Must identify an X11 session for the global backend.
.TP
.B KEYSWITCH_HUNSPELL_PATH
Optional colon-separated list of Hunspell dictionary directories.
.TP
.B KEYSWITCH_MODEL_PATH
Optional colon-separated list of Onboard language-model directories. Entries
precede the bundled frozen EN/RU models and are intended for controlled testing.
.TP
.B KEYSWITCH_INTENT_MODEL_PATH
Optional path to a compatible KSLM schema 4 model. Invalid or oversized files
are rejected and the deterministic detector remains available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setxkbmap (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/olegius88/keyswitch/issues.
